<p>Excellently written but I found the ideas shown being somewhat mediocre, average times for each growth stage would be a nice start, &quot;Dawn Farm and Ranch prides themselves in providing healthy, slightly genetically modified food to our consumers.&quot; seems foolish and unnecessary, the researcher could have asked about his old name as well as designation(wait nm he did), he could have also asked about SCP-1255-1's remembered history, &quot;SCP-1255-1 will no longer require energy from food and rather gain energy from photosynthesis.&quot; could be moved to stage 2 as that's when leaves actually start growing and it becomes still because it would otherwise not provide nearly enough energy and that should atleast be mentioned, how do they pick if their fingernails have woven together(does it come off?)? 20 times should probably be an approximate and would still take several months to grow that much anyway, and how does the seed get all the way to the brain without getting stuck?.</p>
<p>Also I really liked the interview, if anything it was a bit brief, tones nice, how SCP-1255-1 speaks is a bit unsettling and the tactics of it are nicely evident yet you could see how you'd be taken in by a casual conversation with this guy if had no reason to be suspicious which is a nice bit of subtlety that's hard to do.</p>

