<p>1. The seeds are microscopic and trick the body into allowing them to travel through the bloodstream, so my idea was that it would travel through the body until it eventually lodged itself inside the brain.</p>
<p>2. I included the bit about the Farm because, in my own head, Dawn Farm and Ranch is just an anomalous agriculture company that only wants to distribute their produce. It's a bit like Dr. Wondertainment in one way or another. They aren't lying when they say that it is &quot;slightly genetically modified&quot;.</p>
<p>3. My idea for including the photosynthesis bit in stage 1 was that they already were becoming plant people, as I said the veins already became green. I didn't really think that there had to be leaves in order for photosynthesis to start.</p>
<p>4. As for the fingernails bit I didn't really do a lot of research on that. I'll look up some stuff on it later this week and edit that bit.</p>
<p>5. I didn't feel the need to say exactly when each growth stage began? It didn't feel necessary imo since it already said that the time frame is 1 week to 1 month. There is no exact time frame for each cycle, if anything all I could do is an average time frame which just seems unnecessary.</p>
<p>While it gives me sorrow to see that this article has a much lower score than what I would have hoped for, I do understand that it has several problems. What I think I may do if this doesn't gain any traction is just delete it from this slot and work on it for a couple more weeks and maybe repost it to this series II slot if I get lucky.</p>

